# {{.Name}}

A Cobra-based CLI built with [Forge](https://github.com/reliant-labs/forge).

## Quick start

```bash
# Install dependencies
task deps

# Build the binary into ./bin/{{.Name}}
task build

# Run from source
go run ./cmd/{{.Name}} version

# Or install onto $PATH
task install
{{.Name}} version
```

## Adding a subcommand

Each subcommand lives in its own file under `cmd/{{.Name}}/`. The pattern
mirrors `version.go`:

```go
// cmd/{{.Name}}/hello.go
package main

import (
	"fmt"

	"github.com/spf13/cobra"
)

var helloCmd = &cobra.Command{
	Use:   "hello [name]",
	Short: "Print a greeting",
	Args:  cobra.MaximumNArgs(1),
	Run: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) {
		name := "world"
		if len(args) > 0 {
			name = args[0]
		}
		fmt.Printf("hello, %s\n", name)
	},
}

func init() {
	rootCmd.AddCommand(helloCmd)
}
```

For larger commands, factor logic into `internal/<package>/` and call it
from the cobra `Run` function. `forge scaffold package <name>` scaffolds an
internal package with a contract interface and tests.

## Task commands

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `task build` | Build the CLI binary into `./bin/{{.Name}}` |
| `task install` | Install the CLI into `$GOBIN` |
| `task test` | Run `go test ./...`, recording the lane and its coverage under `.forge/tests/runs/` |
| `task test:report` | Summarise the last run |
| `task lint` | Run `golangci-lint` |
| `task fmt` | Run `goimports -w` and `go mod tidy` |
| `task vet` | Run `go vet ./...` |
| `task clean` | Remove `./bin` and coverage outputs |

Run `task --list` (or just `task`) for the full set.

## Test results and coverage

`task test` records every lane it runs, with its coverage, under
`.forge/tests/runs/` (gitignored); `task test:report` summarises the last
run. `FORGE_TESTS=off` records nothing for one run.

CI's "Report test results" step uploads the run to your project's control
plane when the repository secret `FORGE_CONTROL_PLANE_TOKEN` holds a token with
the `tests:write` scope. Mint one while signed in to the web app under
Settings → API tokens (Reliant cloud:
https://forge.reliantlabs.io/settings/tokens), then store it:

```bash
gh secret set FORGE_CONTROL_PLANE_TOKEN
```

Without the secret the step prints one line and stays green; it never
decides the job's result. A token with `deploy:write` also uploads.
`tests.upload: never` in `forge.yaml` turns upload off.

## Project structure

```
{{.Name}}/
├── cmd/{{.Name}}/    # Cobra root + subcommands (each in its own file)
├── internal/         # Application packages (forge scaffold package <name>)
├── pkg/config/       # Configuration types (extend as needed)
├── .reliant/         # Forge conventions, skills, project metadata
├── forge.yaml        # Forge project manifest (kind: cli)
├── go.mod
├── README.md
└── Taskfile.yml
```

## Build flags

Stamp the binary's version, commit, and date at build time so
`{{.Name}} version` reports a real release rather than `dev`:

```bash
go build -trimpath -buildvcs=true \
  -ldflags="-X main.version=v1.0.0 -X main.commit=$(git rev-parse HEAD) -X main.date=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)" \
  -o bin/{{.Name}} ./cmd/{{.Name}}
```
